[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://Scenes/Objects/cables/link_port.tscn" id="1_base"]

; The original Game Boy's EXT. socket: the large Game Link connector. The Pocket,
; the Color, the Advance and the Game Boy Printer (a Pocket-era accessory) kept the
; pin assignment and the smaller shell, so their leads do not go in here and a
; DMG-04 does not go into them -- a small lead reaches this socket through the
; DMG-14 adapter (gb_link_adapter.tscn).
;
; The mouth is the Game Boy's 12.4 x 5.9 mm, drawn 1 mm proud all round as the
; small socket is; the ghost is the DMG-04's body (dmg_link_cable.tscn). Sizes
; from RetroXR-models' MEASUREMENTS.md for nintendo/gb/link-plug and
; nintendo/gbc/universal-link-adapter (read off photographs, scaled by the nose).
